          "transcript": "you're on a GLP-1, more fiber isn't helping your constipation. It's making it worse. Here's why. As a gastroenterologist, I see this on the shot every day. The bloating, the heaviness, the backed up feeling that won't quit. It's called a bile drought. Essentially, what's happening is the shot cut your appetite so hard that your body stopped releasing bile, the fluid that keeps your gut slick and moving. Without it, everything dries out, turns hard, and gets stuck. And honestly, for a lot of women, it only gets worse the longer they stay on the shot. Now here's where most women go wrong. They grab more fiber. And I get it. It's easy. And it's what everyone tells you to do. But in a dried out gut, fiber just clumps into a hard plug and you end up more bloated and backed up than when you started. And Miralax, well, it forces water in to soften one block, but you dry right back out. And most women on a GLP-1 aren't looking to get hooked on something they have to keep taking just to go. Neither one fixes the real problem, the bile that stopped flowing. What I recommend instead is getting your bile flowing again. It's the fluid that keeps your gut slick. And once it's back, everything moves through on its own. Women tell me they're going regularly again within the first few days. And that's how quickly you can see a difference. Here's the catch. Your body makes bile when you eat, especially bitter greens, beets, and healthy fats. But on a GLP-1, you're barely eating, so nothing's telling your liver to release any. That's why I recommend Omyo. It takes those same bile-stimulating foods you can't eat enough of anymore and concentrates them into two capsules. So your liver starts releasing bile again, even when you're eating next to nothing. It uses concentrated bile herbs, milk thistle, artichoke, dandelion, and beet to get your bile moving far better than fiber or water ever could. So your gut goes back to feeling slick, light, and finely regular. 